# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Grocery backend — module-local configuration
#
# ConfigModule loads this file first, then falls back to apps/api/.env for the
# ~120 platform-wide values (Redis, Kafka brokers, JWT secret, region config)
# that every service shares. Only variables this module owns belong here.
#
# Copy to `.env` and adjust. Anything set here overrides the platform file.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Dedicated database ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Grocery owns its data. These GROCERY_DB_* values take precedence over
# the shared DB_* ones; any left unset falls back to the platform database, so a
# partial override is a valid way to run against shared Postgres with a
# different database name.
#
# The schema inside is always `grocery` — that is fixed in the module, not
# configurable, so the same entity definitions work whether this points at a
# dedicated instance or at the shared one.
# Defaults to the module's own Postgres on :5434, brought up by
#   docker compose --profile isolated up -d
# To run against shared Postgres instead, set port 5432 and the postgres
# superuser — the schema name is unchanged either way.
GROCERY_DB_HOST=127.0.0.1
GROCERY_DB_PORT=5434
GROCERY_DB_USER=grocery_user
GROCERY_DB_PASSWORD=change_me_in_development
GROCERY_DB_NAME=kartseek_grocery

# ── Schema source ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Off, and refused if you turn it on. Two guards, no dev escape hatch:
#   • validateDatabaseConfig() in main.ts throws on DB_SYNCHRONIZE=true in EVERY
#     environment, this one included;
#   • assertSynchronizeAllowed() in the TypeORM factory throws if auto-sync
#     reaches it under NODE_ENV=production (reachable when SKIP_DB=true has
#     skipped the first guard).
#
# The schema comes from migrations/ and nothing else:
#
#     cd modules/grocery/backend && npm run migration:show && npm run migration:run
#
# To iterate on entities, generate a migration against a scratch database —
# docs/guides/database-migrations.md, "Generating a migration". Auto-sync is not
# an option there either: it rewrites the schema from the entity definitions on
# every boot, and annotating an existing column is enough to make it DROP and
# recreate that column, which empties it.
DB_SYNCHRONIZE=false

# ── Transport ports ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Kept identical to the values the API gateway's client registrations default
# to. Changing one here means changing GROCERY_TCP_PORT / GROCERY_GRPC_URL
# on the gateway side too, or calls will silently go to the wrong place.
GROCERY_SERVICE_PORT=3018
GROCERY_TCP_PORT=4008
GROCERY_GRPC_PORT=5010
